**Date:** 30 October 2026 · **Deciders:** support desk · **Replaces:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)

## Context

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every date report into one ticket because the subject lines
matched. The reports had two causes, and the queued fix covers only one
([the split](/kb/incidents/4471-causes)).

## Decision

Two reports are the same issue when they share a cause: the tenant's locale and booking form, read
by `causes.ts`. The subject line and the intake tag do not decide it. Count each report id once.

## Consequences

- One ticket per cause, each with its own count and fix.
- Triage needs the tenant directory, not only the subject. `DedupeExplorer` already shows the rule.
